                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 544.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.—Instructions for Mr. Holcombe in regard to
                        the harbor rules.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 6,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>By request of the diplomatic body, Sir Thomas Wade has arranged for you to visit
                    the Tsung-li Yamên to-morrow to speak about the Shanghai Harbor rules.</p>
                <p>The wish of the several ministers is that you ask the ministers of the Yamên
                    simply whether they have anything to communicate to us in “regard to the rules
                    in question in advance of a formal correspondence upon the subject, and in such
                    case to let you know what it is.</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
